          {
            "text": "I wrote `{\"invariant_exists\": false}` to the answer file. I worked this out by reading the code; nothing was run.\n\n**Why it's false:** in `Match._process_match_cases` (`reflex/components/core/match.py:150-160`), `case_list` is reset to an empty list for each case. Then `case_list.append(el)` runs once for every element of `case`, including the first.\n\n- **First append of any case:** `len(case_list)` is 0. The check at line 145 already rejected tuples with fewer than 2 elements, so `len(case) - 1` is at least 1. The relationship `len(case_list) == len(case) - 1` fails here.\n- **Only exception:** it holds only right before the last append of each case, when `case_list` has `len(case) - 1` items.\n\nThe first append happens for every case, so it breaks the relationship whenever the tests call this method with a valid case. I didn't read the test file, so I haven't confirmed that at least one test does. It's very likely, since that's the method's normal path.\n\n**Google Drive:** the claude.ai Google Drive connector needs to be authorized in your claude.ai connector settings before it can be used. It wasn't needed for this task.",
